    "|Use the following information: \nReceipts and Payments Account [Extract]\nReceipts: Balance b/d ₦4,000; Subscriptions received ?; Donations received ₦6,000; Refreshment sales ₦10,000\nPayments: Motor vehicle expenses ₦12,000; Insurance ₦3,000; Ambulance expenses ₦12,500; Electricity ₦1,000; Balance c/d ?\nSubscriptions received are always put at 125% of the total donations received and refreshment sales.\n\nCompute the subscriptions received.|₦30,000|₦28,000|₦24,000|₦20,000": "not-for-profit",
    "|Use the following information: \n(Total / Dept. P / Dept. Q)\nSales ... ₦10,000 / ₦6,000 / ₦4,000\nPurchases ... ₦4,000 / ₦1,000 / ₦3,000\nDiscount received ... ₦1,000 / ? / -\nDiscounts allowed ... ₦2,000 / - / ?\nDiscounts (allowed and received) are apportioned to the two departments on the basis of departmental sales and purchases.\n\nDepartment P's share of discount received is|₦750|₦1,000|₦250|₦500": "departmental-accounts",
